L0@P0: 412.571 CONTINUANCE IN OFFICE; ELECTIONS.
L1@P0: Subdivision 1. Composition of council. When an optional plan is first adopted in any statutory city in
L2@P0: which the standard plan of statutory city government is then in operation, the council shall continue as then
L3@P0: constituted until the expiration of the term of the incumbent clerk. At the city election preceding expiration
L4@P0: of the term of the incumbent clerk, one council member shall be elected in addition to the council member
L5@P0: or council members who would otherwise be chosen at the election. If a minority of the other council members
L6@P0: is chosen at the election, the term of the additional council member chosen at the election shall be four years,
L7@P0: but if a majority of the other council members is chosen at the election, the initial term of the additional
L8@P0: council member chosen at the election shall be two years. At each regular election thereafter, council members
L9@P0: shall be elected for four-year terms. If the optional plan is adopted at the regular city election at which the
L10@P0: office of clerk is to be filled, the candidate elected to that office at the election shall not assume the office
L11@P0: of clerk in January, butshall become the additional council member unless appointed clerk under the optional
L12@P0: plan, in which case the unfilled office of council member shall be considered vacant.
L13@P0: Subd. 2. Incumbent clerk and treasurer. When an optional plan is first adopted in any city in which
L14@P0: the standard plan is then in operation, the incumbent clerk and treasurer, or clerk-treasurer, shall continue
L15@P0: to serve until the expiration of their respective terms.
L16@P0: Subd. 3. From one option to another. When an optional plan is abandoned and another optional plan
L17@P0: is adopted in its place, incumbent members of the council shall continue to serve until the expiration of their
L18@P0: respective terms, and the election schedule shall not be affected by the change.
L19@P0: Subd. 4. From one option to standard plan. When any optional plan is abandoned and the standard
L20@P0: form of city government is resumed, terms of then incumbent council members shall not be affected by the
L21@P0: abandonment; but until the first business day of January following the next regular city election, the clerk
L22@P0: shall not serve as a member of the council. At the city election preceding that date one council member less
L23@P0: shall be elected.
L24@P0: Subd. 5. Standard plan restored; clerk, treasurer. When any optional plan is abandoned and the
L25@P0: standard form of city government is resumed, the office of clerk, or clerk-treasurer shall remain appointive
L26@P0: until the first business day of January following the next regular city election and the office of treasurer, if
L27@P0: there is no clerk-treasurer, shall remain appointive until the first business day of January following the first
L28@P0: subsequent city election at which the clerk is not elected; and the successor to the incumbent clerk,
L29@P0: clerk-treasurer, and treasurer shall be chosen at the regular city election immediately preceding the January
L30@P0: in which the office becomes elective.
L31@P0: History: 1949 c 119 s 73; 1951 c 378 s 15-17; 1965 c 417 s 9,10; 1967 c 289 s 12; 1973 c 123 art 2 s
L32@P0: 1 subd 2; 1976 c 44 s 28-30; 1986 c 444; 1989 c 30 s 7,8
